sentences.l:
Coming out and going down one step,
he let his face relax, and was at ease;
at the foot of the steps, hastening forward, winglike he was;
back in his place, reverent and uneasy he was.

Holding the tablet,
bent low he was,
as if he could not bear it.
High, as in bowing; low, as in handing over;
his face changed, as if trembling;
his feet in short steps, as if following something.

With a black robe, lambskin;
with a white robe, fawnskin;
with a yellow robe, fox fur.

Kangzi sent him medicine;
he bowed and accepted it, and said:
“I, Qiu, do not yet understand it;
I do not venture to taste it.”
